WEBVTT

00:12.300 --> 00:14.200
The date for the large-scale event,

00:14.750 --> 00:18.430
Tempest Founder's Festival,
has been officially decided.

00:18.960 --> 00:21.050
Everyone is busy preparing for that.

00:27.000 --> 00:31.300
Each of the executives is set
to announce some kind of project.

00:32.100 --> 00:33.890
History of healing potion?

00:33.890 --> 00:36.310
Indeed so, Great Rimuru!

00:36.310 --> 00:39.390
Sir Vester and I will hold
a presentation on these

00:39.390 --> 00:42.690
healing potions we worked
so hard together to improve!

00:43.120 --> 00:46.480
All the crucial information will be
a trade secret, so rest assured.

00:46.480 --> 00:50.780
The purpose is to attract people
who'd like to participate in the research.

00:50.780 --> 00:54.080
Oh, I see. It'd be a great opportunity
to gather more collaborators.

00:54.080 --> 00:55.080
Do your best.

00:55.080 --> 00:58.580
Of course we will, sir!
We won't lose to Sir Kurobe!

00:58.580 --> 01:02.330
Oh, yeah. I heard they plan to show off
their best work at the event.

01:02.700 --> 01:05.630
We're competing to see which of us
will attract the most visitors.

01:05.630 --> 01:07.760
It's a festival, after all.

01:07.760 --> 01:10.260
Yup! It'll be a waste not to enjoy it!

01:10.970 --> 01:13.510
I'm glad everyone is excited about it.

01:17.220 --> 01:18.520
What's the matter, Shion?

01:18.520 --> 01:20.140
Have you decided on your project?

01:20.140 --> 01:23.240
Please look forward to it, Great Rimuru!

01:23.900 --> 01:25.610
That sounds ominous.

01:26.130 --> 01:27.440
Oh, that reminds me.

01:30.070 --> 01:32.530
I just came up with the best idea!

01:32.530 --> 01:34.820
I'll do a teppanyaki booth
using my Dragon Brea—

01:37.200 --> 01:38.700
I'll forget that for now.

01:42.230 --> 01:43.580
What's the matter, Shuna?

01:44.080 --> 01:45.590
Here to consult about your project?

01:45.590 --> 01:48.710
Um, I'd like to ask for your assistance.

01:51.010 --> 01:54.520
Please take me to Engrassia!

02:59.450 --> 03:03.200
THAT TIME I GOT REINCARNATED AS A SLIME

03:24.980 --> 03:26.810
KINGDOM OF ENGRASSIA

03:26.810 --> 03:28.690
EPISODE 60: THE PREPARATION
As much as I'd love to,

03:28.690 --> 03:30.690
EPISODE 60: THE PREPARATION
I can't easily say yes to that...

03:30.690 --> 03:32.400
This man is Yoshida.

03:32.400 --> 03:36.010
He's an Otherworlder just like me,
as well as a patissier.

03:36.010 --> 03:38.820
We really need your skill as a chef.

03:39.170 --> 03:40.740
Please, come to Tempest.

03:40.740 --> 03:42.650
Before I opened this café,

03:42.650 --> 03:44.790
a great number of people
helped me a ton.

03:44.790 --> 03:48.790
I'd love to give all the help I can,
but I can't leave this place now.

03:49.750 --> 03:51.710
I hope you will reconsider!

03:52.920 --> 03:56.260
Y-Your charm won't
work on me that easily!

03:56.260 --> 03:56.970
Huh?

03:56.970 --> 04:01.850
I-If you want to convince me,
show me your kitchen skill!

04:02.280 --> 04:07.600
I-If you can serve me a satisfactory dish,
I wouldn't mind considering it.

04:08.900 --> 04:11.610
Shuna, show him what you really got!

04:11.610 --> 04:15.110
Make a spectacular dish that would
shock this cocky baker's mind!

04:15.110 --> 04:17.360
Yes, sir!

04:17.360 --> 04:18.820
I'll borrow your kitchen!

04:31.040 --> 04:32.170
It's good!

04:33.690 --> 04:34.960
Thank you very much!

04:34.960 --> 04:37.400
Sheesh, you got me.

04:37.400 --> 04:38.720
Consider this a special favor!

04:39.490 --> 04:40.380
Well, then...

04:40.790 --> 04:43.220
I should go do something myself, too.

04:43.670 --> 04:44.850
Oh, I know!

04:44.850 --> 04:46.100
KINGDOM OF BLUMUND

04:49.350 --> 04:52.520
So, what brings you here today?

04:54.860 --> 04:58.530
I'm thinking of opening
a new shop using slaves.

04:58.530 --> 05:01.330
I'm here to let you invest
in this lucrative business.

05:01.330 --> 05:03.990
Oh, I see. So you're seeking
to open a night establishment?

05:03.990 --> 05:08.870
Then I must ask how much
you will be paying the girls.

05:08.870 --> 05:13.830
Huh? What sort of fool pays their slaves?

05:13.830 --> 05:15.290
This guy's no good.

05:15.290 --> 05:18.970
Besides, does he even know
how much a high-class slave cost?

05:18.970 --> 05:21.970
Yes, indeed, Sir Cazac,
you have a discerning eye.

05:21.970 --> 05:24.890
I must take my hat off to your wisdom.

05:24.890 --> 05:27.220
However, I fear it may
be difficult to procure

05:27.220 --> 05:29.600
those important slaves
at this time, would it not?

05:29.950 --> 05:31.850
Well, about that...

05:31.850 --> 05:34.730
Just between you and me,
I actually have an in.

05:34.730 --> 05:36.360
The slave in question is an elf.

05:37.400 --> 05:38.820
An elf?

05:38.820 --> 05:42.450
It's impossible to turn an elf
who has citizenship into a slave.

05:42.450 --> 05:45.830
That would mean they captured
one hiding in the forest...

05:45.830 --> 05:49.870
Only serious organized crime
would get mixed up in that!

05:49.870 --> 05:52.250
What do you say?
Not a bad deal, don't you think?

05:53.120 --> 05:54.520
Yes, of course, sir!

05:54.520 --> 05:56.150
It'd be bad if I got involved in this.

05:56.150 --> 05:58.250
I need a good excuse
to turn down this offer...

05:58.250 --> 05:59.710
Hello!

05:59.710 --> 06:01.840
- How are you doing, my friend Mjöllmile?
- Hm? Who are you?

06:01.840 --> 06:04.510
How dare you interrupt
my important business meeting!

06:04.510 --> 06:06.890
Oh, my! If it isn't Mr. Rimuru!

06:06.890 --> 06:11.180
I thought you said you were caught
in some crisis and couldn't come to visit?

06:11.180 --> 06:13.850
Oh, sorry.
You're seeing another visitor?

06:13.850 --> 06:16.290
Then I'll wait till you're done.
Later.

06:21.010 --> 06:23.650
Hey, you brat... or a girl?

06:23.650 --> 06:26.690
You came without permission,
listened to confidential information,

06:26.690 --> 06:28.290
and interrupted my business meeting!

06:28.290 --> 06:30.540
How do you plan to pay
for your indiscretion, hmm?

06:30.540 --> 06:34.830
Oh, I apologize for that, sir.
I'm sorry, really.

06:34.830 --> 06:37.670
Hm, you do have quite a fine face.

06:37.670 --> 06:39.380
Hey, Cazac.

06:39.380 --> 06:40.740
Huh?

06:40.740 --> 06:46.510
Anyway, manners are important.
How about I look after you instead?

06:46.510 --> 06:50.680
You are being rude
to the person I owe my life to!

06:50.680 --> 06:54.190
You think a mere viscount such as you
can get away with angering me?

06:54.980 --> 06:56.480
Wh-What did you say?!

06:58.480 --> 07:01.230
There will be no more business between us!

07:01.230 --> 07:03.780
Don't you ever come here
begging me for anything ever again!

07:03.780 --> 07:07.490
H-How dare you! A lowly merchant,
rebelling against a noble...?!

07:07.490 --> 07:11.080
Hmph! Anyone willing to work with
criminal groups is nothing but trouble!

07:11.080 --> 07:13.450
I have no business to do with you,
so leave at once!

07:13.450 --> 07:18.960
M-Mjöllmile, how dare you!
After all the favors I've done for you!

07:18.960 --> 07:22.960
- I'll make you regret this!
- Hmph, like a child thinking he's a big shot.

07:22.960 --> 07:24.920
H-Hey, Mjöllmile?

07:24.920 --> 07:27.970
You sure you're okay
with riling that guy?

07:29.220 --> 07:32.140
You're really something else, Mr. Rimuru.

07:38.900 --> 07:41.690
An elf slave, huh.

07:42.350 --> 07:45.150
Some people out there sure
come out with terrible things.

07:45.150 --> 07:49.660
I had wanted to cut ties with
that dunderhead for a while now.

07:49.660 --> 07:50.950
Would that be okay?

07:50.950 --> 07:55.120
They call me the King of
the Dark City, you know.

07:55.120 --> 07:57.670
I can handle this much myself.

07:57.670 --> 08:02.170
So what brings you here today,
Mr. Rimuru?

08:02.170 --> 08:05.920
Well, I actually got a job
I want your help with.

08:05.920 --> 08:09.840
Oh, another one of your interesting ideas?

08:09.840 --> 08:12.510
All the jobs you bring me
are fascinating,

08:12.510 --> 08:15.310
but it's always a lot of work
to prepare for them.

08:15.310 --> 08:17.940
Like the fast food expansion project?

08:17.940 --> 08:19.100
Precisely!

08:19.100 --> 08:21.320
Oh, don't be like that, Mjöllmile.

08:21.320 --> 08:23.320
About that project,

08:23.320 --> 08:26.820
I actually would like you to open up
a test location in my nation first.

08:26.820 --> 08:31.450
Oh, in that case, let me show you
the results of our training so far!

08:31.450 --> 08:33.950
So the training went well, then?

08:33.950 --> 08:35.620
Yes, of course!

08:35.620 --> 08:40.460
We've trained them to the point that everyone
can perform their tasks on the same level.

08:40.730 --> 08:42.110
That sounds promising.

08:42.110 --> 08:46.710
How about we put up a storefront offering
burgers, fries, and a drink lineup?

08:46.710 --> 08:48.490
That sounds great!

08:48.490 --> 08:50.970
And I think we can attract
quite a number of customers

08:50.970 --> 08:53.680
with those grilled meat skewers
dipped in that "secret sauce."

08:53.680 --> 08:58.980
Pairing them with a rice bowl
will definitely improve our bottom line!

08:58.980 --> 09:00.940
All right,
let's add that to the menu, too!

09:01.560 --> 09:03.980
So, do we have enough
employees to work with?

09:03.980 --> 09:09.210
Well, I'm thinking we could launch
with upward of twenty locations for now.

09:09.210 --> 09:12.170
I invested a lot in the training,
seeing it as a necessary expense,

09:12.170 --> 09:13.780
so I have many men to run things.

09:14.140 --> 09:16.690
Then, sorry to trouble you with this,

09:16.690 --> 09:20.040
but can you bring over around
five of your best employees?

09:20.040 --> 09:23.040
Five? What do you need them for?

09:23.040 --> 09:27.550
Actually, I've got this friend of mine.
His name's Veldora.

09:27.550 --> 09:29.300
V-Veldora...?

09:29.670 --> 09:34.050
And he's super worked up about opening
a teppanyaki booth at the fest.

09:34.050 --> 09:36.810
I-Is he, huh?

09:36.810 --> 09:40.230
So I'm kinda worried about leaving him
running that by himself. You get me?

09:40.230 --> 09:42.020
I-I would feel the same, yes.

09:42.020 --> 09:44.440
So that brings us back to the request.

09:44.440 --> 09:48.320
I want five of your best men to help him!

09:48.320 --> 09:54.200
Would you be able to guarantee their...
Err... safety and stuff?

09:54.200 --> 09:55.490
Of course!

09:55.490 --> 09:59.120
If he gets all uppity,
I'll be sure to yell at him.

09:59.120 --> 10:01.410
I do trust you on that, but...

10:01.410 --> 10:02.900
Is there a problem?

10:02.900 --> 10:08.710
Not exactly a problem, but I fear they'd
be too scared to focus on their work.

10:08.710 --> 10:12.340
Yeah, if you haven't met him,
you must find him really scary.

10:12.340 --> 10:14.730
He's a Catastrophe-class, after all.

10:14.730 --> 10:16.850
That's not a good idea, huh?

10:16.850 --> 10:21.180
Let's see... if he could at least
assume another name...

10:21.180 --> 10:23.600
Yes! That's it, Mjöllmile!

10:23.600 --> 10:27.730
I'll have him use a fake name
to hide his identity!

10:27.730 --> 10:30.650
Huh? You can do that?!

10:30.650 --> 10:34.660
Sure. If he whines about it,
I'll just tell him he can't do it.

10:34.660 --> 10:36.410
All right, let's go with that!

10:36.410 --> 10:40.080
I'll pay a special bonus
to those five people,

10:40.080 --> 10:42.910
so let them know
I'm counting on 'em, okay?

10:46.580 --> 10:48.540
Lord Veldora?!

10:48.540 --> 10:50.710
I did hear that his seal
has been undone,

10:50.710 --> 10:53.920
but how come I have to be
the one to deal with him?!

10:54.260 --> 10:57.720
Good grief, things sure have turned
to a whole other level.

10:57.720 --> 10:59.140
Still...

11:03.600 --> 11:07.150
I already die back then,
on that day...

11:08.190 --> 11:13.320
Ever since Mr. Rimuru saved me,
I've tried to live my life with no regrets.

11:13.650 --> 11:17.070
And if he's putting his trust in me...

11:18.620 --> 11:21.000
This is getting interesting.

11:22.450 --> 11:25.910
But still, a festival, though, eh?

11:25.910 --> 11:28.080
If we're talking about
an event of such a scale,

11:28.080 --> 11:30.380
I imagine many people would be
eager to participate.

11:30.380 --> 11:33.960
A good opportunity for a merchant
like myself, I must say.

11:33.960 --> 11:35.840
Oh, are you interested?

11:35.840 --> 11:39.930
To tell you the truth,
I'm still wavering on a few things.

11:39.930 --> 11:42.890
I want something to serve as
our nation's main attraction.

11:43.220 --> 11:44.890
Main attraction?

11:44.890 --> 11:46.190
Yeah!

11:46.190 --> 11:49.310
We're planning to turn our town
into a health resort.

11:49.310 --> 11:51.400
We've got our hot-spring inn,

11:51.400 --> 11:55.440
along with lodging and guest houses
to welcome the royalty.

11:55.440 --> 11:58.160
But I feel like we're still
lacking in entertainment.

11:58.160 --> 11:59.490
I see.

11:59.490 --> 12:02.990
But if you already have good food
and relaxing spaces,

12:02.990 --> 12:06.160
how much more of a resort do you need?

12:06.160 --> 12:08.250
You aren't thinking big enough, Mjöllmile.

12:08.250 --> 12:10.630
I think that won't be enough on its own.

12:10.630 --> 12:13.920
I want something that everyone can enjoy.

12:14.250 --> 12:15.460
For example...

12:17.590 --> 12:20.510
A tour into the Forest of Jura
accompanied by a guide!

12:21.760 --> 12:23.750
A fishing tournaments
at the mountain stream.

12:24.770 --> 12:27.140
And a hunting event, too.

12:27.140 --> 12:31.520
I'm thinking of making the needed equipment
available for rent to anyone interested.

12:31.520 --> 12:33.690
That sounds fun!

12:33.690 --> 12:36.940
The nobles who have too much time
on their hands would love it!

12:36.940 --> 12:39.610
It'd be a fine way
for regular citizens to relax, too.

12:39.610 --> 12:43.650
I was wondering if there are
any other ideas like that.

12:44.330 --> 12:47.660
I personally want to make those who come
to the Founder's Festival

12:47.660 --> 12:50.500
come back again as repeat visitors.

12:50.500 --> 12:51.880
And to make that happen,

12:51.880 --> 12:55.500
I need to prepare many activities
to keep them engaged and interested.

12:55.500 --> 12:59.760
Just how far ahead in the future
is he thinking?

12:59.760 --> 13:03.350
I heard the theater is
popular in Engrassia.

13:03.350 --> 13:06.600
They hold operas and stage plays
nearly every day there.

13:06.600 --> 13:10.310
There are also fighting tournaments
held at the arena—

13:10.310 --> 13:12.060
Oooh! I know that!

13:12.060 --> 13:14.980
I heard the Hero Masayuki
is really popular there!

13:14.980 --> 13:16.730
Yes, that's right!

13:16.730 --> 13:19.190
Sir Masayuki, known as the Lightspeed,

13:19.190 --> 13:21.780
is the dominating champion
of the tournaments!

13:21.780 --> 13:24.240
I'm actually a big fan of his!

13:24.240 --> 13:25.240
What?

13:25.240 --> 13:27.910
Want me to tell you about
the Hero Masayuki?

13:27.910 --> 13:31.870
I can tell you all about him!
I hope you're prepared for it!

13:31.870 --> 13:33.790
O-Oh, sure.

13:34.500 --> 13:39.510
And like that, nobody has ever seen
the flash of his sword!

13:39.510 --> 13:42.590
That's how people gave him
the name "Lightspeed"!

13:42.590 --> 13:45.470
They also battle captured monsters,

13:45.470 --> 13:48.220
and the Hero's companions
are pretty strong themselves!

13:48.220 --> 13:50.870
It was a real white-knuckle match,
I tell you!

13:50.870 --> 13:52.850
If Tempest has something like that, then...

13:52.850 --> 13:55.860
Oh, I apologize.
I have gotten a bit heated up.

13:55.860 --> 13:59.360
But the idea itself is interesting.

13:59.360 --> 14:03.280
There is one vacant section in the town.
We could turn it into an opera house.

14:03.280 --> 14:06.030
Some might want to become
playwrights thanks to it,

14:06.030 --> 14:08.620
and that'd lead to some
new forms of entertainment!

14:08.620 --> 14:11.000
And an arena, eh?

14:11.540 --> 14:15.040
Oh, he's scheming about something again.

14:15.040 --> 14:16.250
Mjöllmile!

14:16.250 --> 14:17.540
Wh-What is it, sir?

14:17.540 --> 14:20.800
You know a lot about
battle tournaments, right?

14:20.800 --> 14:22.470
Y-Yeah...

14:22.470 --> 14:27.180
I'll hold one in Tempest,
so can you arrange that for me?

14:27.180 --> 14:29.850
W-Wait just a minute!

14:29.850 --> 14:33.590
You can't just say something
so important so suddenly like that...

14:35.190 --> 14:37.770
We'll build the arena for you.

14:37.770 --> 14:42.440
For now, I just need you to look up
the stuff needed to hold a show.

14:42.440 --> 14:43.790
Every single time,

14:43.790 --> 14:46.030
there's just no beating you,
is there, Mr. Rimuru?

14:46.030 --> 14:47.570
Very well.

14:47.570 --> 14:51.790
I, Mjöllmile, shall do my best
to meet your expectations!

14:51.790 --> 14:53.020
Great!

14:53.020 --> 14:56.040
He might not look like it,
but Mr. Rimuru is a Demon Lord.

14:56.040 --> 14:58.080
As long as his plans are sound,

14:58.080 --> 15:01.590
assembling the stuff he needs
is a simple task.

15:01.590 --> 15:03.800
And he's relying on me for that!

15:04.590 --> 15:08.050
I've got to do it! This kind of opportunity
only comes once in a lifetime!

15:08.050 --> 15:12.310
Oh, also, the fest's purpose is
to welcome the world leaders,

15:12.310 --> 15:15.690
You can't make a profit if it's not open
to the general public, after all.

15:15.690 --> 15:17.650
The general public?

15:17.650 --> 15:18.190
Yup.

15:18.530 --> 15:22.230
I'm planning to build a coliseum capable of
holding fifty thousand people or so.

15:22.230 --> 15:24.610
F-Fifty thousand?!

15:25.740 --> 15:28.200
It's absurd, no matter how you spin it!

15:28.200 --> 15:32.740
Fifty thousand?! That's five times
the one in Engrassia!

15:32.740 --> 15:36.360
We'll have some standing-room sections
and make it free of charge.

15:36.360 --> 15:39.920
We can direct rich people to the reserved
seats and charge them appropriately.

15:39.920 --> 15:44.010
It'll be VIP seats for nobility
who have no financial worries.

15:44.010 --> 15:48.140
So I'd like you to figure out the ratios
we need for all these seat types.

15:48.140 --> 15:49.470
Oh, I see.

15:49.470 --> 15:53.680
I thought fifty thousand was too much,
but now I understand what you're after.

15:53.680 --> 15:54.600
Yeah.

15:54.600 --> 15:57.990
It's important to attract people's
interest in this kind of stuff.

15:57.990 --> 16:00.250
And when the standing-room
sections are all packed,

16:00.250 --> 16:02.370
a reserved seat
where you can sit and relax

16:02.370 --> 16:04.400
would look more attractive,
don't you think?

16:04.400 --> 16:05.780
I bet it would.

16:05.780 --> 16:08.490
Rather than space you don't
know will be available,

16:08.490 --> 16:13.620
seats that you can reserve in advance
will naturally be more valuable.

16:13.620 --> 16:14.880
There you have it.

16:14.880 --> 16:18.000
This is a fundamentally different approach
from the arena in Engrassia,

16:18.000 --> 16:20.630
which was solely for
the entertainment of the upper classes.

16:20.630 --> 16:22.380
The aim here was to build buzz.

16:22.380 --> 16:25.590
In other words, to pack as
many people in as possible.

16:25.950 --> 16:28.090
And traffic of tens of
thousands of people

16:28.090 --> 16:30.260
would no doubt fill up the inns
along the highways.

16:30.260 --> 16:33.310
It'd be a great way to advertise
Tempest's food and baths!

16:33.310 --> 16:37.680
That means the arena itself
wouldn't even need to make a profit!

16:37.680 --> 16:39.310
I gotta hand it to you, Mr. Rimuru!

16:39.310 --> 16:41.860
You had this all planned out
from the start, didn't you?

16:43.270 --> 16:46.210
Hmph, of course I do!

16:46.210 --> 16:47.900
I came out with it on the fly, though.

16:48.360 --> 16:53.080
We'll need to boost our profit margins later,
but spreading the word comes first.

16:53.080 --> 16:57.750
And you're counting on me
to help with that first step, yes?

16:57.750 --> 16:59.540
Y-Yeah, that's right.

16:59.540 --> 17:01.370
I see, I see.

17:01.370 --> 17:03.290
You want me to come up
with an entertainment

17:03.290 --> 17:05.090
that'll bring people
back again and again.

17:05.090 --> 17:08.340
And even if this particular battle
tournament turns out a loss,

17:08.340 --> 17:12.260
if we managed to make
people want to come again,

17:12.260 --> 17:14.890
you'll consider the project a success?

17:14.890 --> 17:18.310
I'm impressed you understand me so well.

17:18.310 --> 17:22.770
I knew it, Mjöllmile.
You're the only man I can trust with this job!

17:22.770 --> 17:25.570
Heh, heh-heh,
you're thinking too highly of me.

17:25.570 --> 17:27.970
All right, just a little more push.

17:27.970 --> 17:30.470
It's best to leave this to a professional, right?

17:30.470 --> 17:32.200
Don't tell me you have no confidence?

17:33.780 --> 17:37.210
Oh, how harsh. You can be quite mean,
aren't you, Mr. Rimuru?

17:38.810 --> 17:42.000
I knew you would say that!
This is a piece of cake for you, isn't it?

17:42.460 --> 17:44.420
You do realize, do you?

17:45.880 --> 17:47.070
Not to worry.

17:47.070 --> 17:50.670
You have Mjöllmile on your side,
and accounting is my specialty.

17:50.670 --> 17:54.760
I'm sure I can give you exactly
the results you want!

17:54.760 --> 17:56.260
I'm sure you will.

17:56.260 --> 17:58.810
I knew counting on you
was the right thing to do.

18:05.560 --> 18:10.570
Now, this also means we have
a new way to use your healing potions.

18:10.570 --> 18:11.320
Hm?

18:12.110 --> 18:16.660
They can heal you as long
as you didn't die instantly, yes?

18:16.660 --> 18:20.620
That means our competitors
don't have to hold back in fights.

18:20.620 --> 18:24.750
Plus, if one is injured in one match
and appears as good as new in the next one,

18:24.750 --> 18:27.210
that would certainly make
for some good advertising!

18:27.210 --> 18:28.130
What did you say?!

18:28.130 --> 18:31.380
Oh, you haven't thought of it that far?

18:31.380 --> 18:33.380
No, of course I have!

18:33.380 --> 18:39.250
I just wanted to see if your idea
was any different from mine.

18:39.250 --> 18:40.890
I didn't think of it that way at all.

18:40.890 --> 18:42.770
Ah, I see!

18:43.350 --> 18:47.810
Yes, I'm sure you've already
considered that much, Mr. Rimuru.

18:47.810 --> 18:49.900
But I'm not giving up just yet!

18:49.900 --> 18:53.900
Also, maybe we can show weapons and armor
made in Tempest to Adventurers.

18:53.900 --> 18:56.780
Or a state-run betting operations?

18:56.780 --> 18:58.160
And when there's no event,

18:58.160 --> 19:00.810
we can rent out the arena
for beginner Adventurers' training!

19:00.810 --> 19:03.830
If we're doing that, let's add instructors
and make offer paid lessons!

19:03.830 --> 19:05.120
Oh, that's nice!

19:05.120 --> 19:07.380
I'll do it.
I'll do it all for you!

19:07.380 --> 19:12.380
My merchant's soul is telling me there's
a massive pile of money to make from this!

19:12.380 --> 19:18.010
Excellent! I know you got what it takes
to give me the kind of revenue I want!

19:18.010 --> 19:19.970
Awww!

19:19.970 --> 19:22.350
Also, only if you're interested,
of course...

19:22.350 --> 19:22.950
Hm?

19:22.950 --> 19:26.010
If this whole tournament turns out well,
do you wanna come live in my town?

19:26.010 --> 19:26.520
What?

19:26.850 --> 19:29.270
You can be in charge of
the trade or PR department,

19:29.270 --> 19:31.530
or even the general finance department.

19:31.530 --> 19:34.110
But well, any title will do.

19:34.110 --> 19:36.910
I want you to be in charge of that.

19:36.910 --> 19:37.910
You want me in charge?

19:38.290 --> 19:40.700
We've gotten pretty big as a nation now,

19:40.700 --> 19:44.750
so once the tournament's over,
I'd like to reorganize our administration.

19:45.160 --> 19:46.320
What do you say?

19:47.830 --> 19:50.250
There's just no beating you, Mr. Rimuru.

19:50.250 --> 19:52.090
No, Great Rimuru.

19:55.090 --> 19:59.260
I promise you I'll do whatever it takes
to make this project a success

19:59.890 --> 20:04.020
and fully join you as one of
your subordinates.

20:05.350 --> 20:07.930
You don't have to exaggerate it
that much, Mjöllmile.

20:12.320 --> 20:13.820
Next's this.

20:13.820 --> 20:17.270
Hellooooo! I'm here to visit!

20:19.530 --> 20:23.540
What's wrong? Something up?
Why the long face?

20:23.540 --> 20:27.000
Well, things were
pretty peaceful just now,

20:27.000 --> 20:29.330
but this Demon Lord
came out from nowhere...

20:29.330 --> 20:31.460
Whoa, really?
Sounds like bad news.

20:36.010 --> 20:39.380
I'm sorry about everything
that happened, Sir Rimuru.

20:39.380 --> 20:42.510
My attempt to hold the Western
Holy Church down didn't work too well,

20:42.510 --> 20:45.430
and the Crusaders got deployed anyway.

20:46.020 --> 20:48.710
Nah, I don't think there was
anything you could do.

20:48.710 --> 20:52.310
Apparently this band called the Seven Days Clergy
was masterminding the whole thing.

20:53.610 --> 20:59.950
So I'm sure the Church wouldn't have listened
anyway no matter what you say to them.

20:59.950 --> 21:01.490
The Seven Days...

21:01.490 --> 21:06.200
You mean those once great heroes
and the guardians of humanity?

21:06.200 --> 21:07.750
Apparently, yeah.

21:07.750 --> 21:09.460
They also shot through Hinata.

21:09.460 --> 21:11.790
Well, a lot happened,
but she's fine now.

21:11.790 --> 21:13.730
Anyway, the misunderstanding
is cleared now.

21:13.730 --> 21:14.710
Is that so?

21:14.710 --> 21:18.600
Well, hearing that at least
lift some load off my chest.

21:19.630 --> 21:23.470
He's worried about me that much?
What a good guy.

21:25.010 --> 21:26.810
Anyway, I'll be going now.

21:27.430 --> 21:28.810
So here, take this.

21:29.170 --> 21:30.060
What's this?

21:30.060 --> 21:33.610
I'm going to be holding
my Demon Lord coronation soon,

21:33.610 --> 21:37.230
and we're going to use the opportunity
to advertise my town to the world.

21:37.230 --> 21:39.190
I'd love it if you could come too.

21:39.190 --> 21:43.410
Huh? Wait a minute, Sir Rimuru.
Why are you inviting someone like me...

21:43.410 --> 21:44.910
What's the big deal?

21:44.910 --> 21:48.540
The invitation for the king of Blumund is
in that, too, so can you deliver it to him?

21:48.920 --> 21:51.830
It'd be bad if a Demon Lord were
to hand deliver it himself, right?

21:51.830 --> 21:55.340
It's bad enough for a Demon Lord
to be in here at all.

21:56.170 --> 21:59.090
But I understand.

21:59.090 --> 22:01.420
I'll be sure this reaches the king.

22:01.420 --> 22:03.180
Great. See you later.

22:03.180 --> 22:07.680
Oh, right.
Grandmaster was concerned about you.

22:09.270 --> 22:10.270
Yuuki did?

22:10.270 --> 22:14.190
He went through quite a lot to negotiate
with the Western Holy Church,

22:14.190 --> 22:17.020
so I'll be sure to say
you've worked things out.

22:17.020 --> 22:20.280
I see.
I must have put a lot on his plate.

22:20.280 --> 22:22.320
I don't think he would think so.

22:22.320 --> 22:24.280
But I should thank him somehow.

22:24.280 --> 22:27.240
Oh, right! Do you think he'd mind
if I invited him too?

22:27.240 --> 22:28.490
Hard to say.

22:28.490 --> 22:32.290
Not that I can speak for him,
but he is a busy man.

22:32.640 --> 22:34.930
I can give him an escort
to and from the event.

22:34.930 --> 22:36.460
I'm sure we can work it out.

22:37.190 --> 22:40.670
Anyway, please give this to him for me.

22:40.670 --> 22:42.660
Sure thing, Sir Rimuru.

22:43.760 --> 22:45.430
Oh, also...

22:45.780 --> 22:47.800
Milim will be coming
to the festival, too.

22:47.800 --> 22:49.010
Milim?

22:49.010 --> 22:50.760
Huh?! You mean...

22:50.760 --> 22:53.020
Okay, see you there!

22:53.020 --> 22:53.940
Wait—

22:56.560 --> 22:59.940
You don't mean
the Demon Lord Milim, do you?

22:59.940 --> 23:05.320
Now, all that's left is to get things ready
before the day of the festival.

24:35.950 --> 24:39.330
Next time,
"The Nations and Invitations."
